itda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":78.7,"_gate_accruals":-0.04714258225899558,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":33.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.19010583801362063,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":60.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.26964905071929224,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":0.20894091080429367,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.002870234009476419,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":32.4,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.06305549390912557,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.5170674746864026,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.026184301071033034,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":76.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0.04237900313026728,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":42.4,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02827413576982424,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":42.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.007042949693310208,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":41.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0077267181781211875,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":87.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.021259999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Weatherford International plc, an energy services company, provides equipment and services for the drilling, evaluation, completion, production, and intervention of oil, geothermal, and natural gas wells worldwide. The company operates through three segments: Drilling and Evaluation; Well Construction and Completions; and Production and Intervention. It offers managed pressure drilling; directional drilling services, and logging and measurement services while drilling; services related to rotary-steerable systems, high temperature and high pressure sensors, drilling reamers, and circulation subs; open-hole and cased-hole logging services; wireline and drilling fluids; and intervention and remediation services. The company also provides tubular handling, management, and connection services; cementing products, including plugs, float and stage equipment, and torque-and-drag reduction technology for zonal isolation; completion tools, such as safety valves, production packers, downhole reservoir monitoring, flow control, isolation packers, multistage fracturing systems and sand-control technologies; liner hangers to suspend a casing string in high-temperature and high-pressure wells; and well Services. In addition, it offers re-entry, fishing, and well abandonment services, as well as patented downhole tools, tubular-handling equipment, pressure-control equipment, and drill pipe and tubulars; artificial lift systems, including reciprocating rod, progressing cavity pumping, and related automation and control systems, as well as gas, hydraulic, plunger, and hybrid lift systems, as well as related automation and control systems; and software, automation and flow measurement solutions. Further, it provides electrical and hydraulic power transmission to subsea equipment; and pressure pumping and reservoir stimulation services, such as acidizing, fracturing, cementing, and coiled-tubing intervention. The company was incorporated in 1972 and is based in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Girishchandra K. Saligram | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $294K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers, declining at 10%/yr \u2014 weakening productivity. Each employee generates $27K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Weatherford International plc is a mid-cap energy business with a $6.1B market cap on $4.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and -6% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 30% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 21-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 18% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $450M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.57\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $17.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-17014827.01},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Energy peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Debt Paydown Change The Bull Case For Weatherford International Stock (WFRD)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-wfrd/weatherford-international/news/does-debt-paydown-change-the-bull-case-for-weatherford-inter","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794011424.038,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to WFRD Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Technical_Reactions_to_WFRD_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_110426085601_1793800561.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793800561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Weatherford International (WFRD) Redeems Debt As Fair Value Debate Meets New Contract Momentum","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-wfrd/weatherford-